<Defs>

  <!--
    The Wheel (docs/design/peoples-next.md, the fourth of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release D";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesD.cs, WheelTowns.cs): the rolling salvage town, circling the region once every few
    years, buying what others throw away and selling it back better. Industrial, on the game's outlander parent; they
    arise in every age (ariseAges 0~3): in the tribal and medieval ages their yard guards carry hammers and maces, in the
    spacer age salvaged lasers (Vanilla Weapons Expanded - Laser) (ageArms). Patched coats, every piece mended
    differently, weathered to the colour of old brass (their signature: the coat of any cut in old brass, the brass cog
    on its shoulder); tool belts (Vanilla Apparel Expanded - Accessories); a mechanitor or two with Biotech's mechlink and
    headset. Their towns are workshop yards and scrap heaps laid out as if leaving tomorrow (Rimfolk_Plan_WheelYard), and
    a Wheel town moves on a few tiles every month or so, as no other people's does (Peoples/WheelTowns.cs). Their
    caravans are the region's most frequent (caravanWeight 2): pack beasts for their carts; with Giddy-Up its own rules
    mount their riders. At the gate: a fixer mends the colony's worn clothes and weapons for silver
    (Rimfolk_Evt_WheelMending); scrap-runners buy slag and broken things and sell a refurbished piece (Rimfolk_Evt_WheelScrap);
    a wrecked mechanoid near the colony brings them at a run (Rimfolk_Evt_WheelWreck). Their ask: parts for a broken axle
    (Rimfolk_Mission_WheelAxle). The travelling tinker and the scrap-pickers' camp come from them likeliest. Their
    founding: Mab Wainwright, who put her house on her cart the night the valley burned and never took it off. Faith
    (Ideology): the town as one (collectivist), salvage (VE Memes' scrapper) and the road (VE Memes' nomad). Kinds of
    people: wasters, dirtmoles, genies, starjacks (Odyssey), VRE's androids, stoneborn, boglegs and Alpha Genes' lapis,
    three in four baseliners.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Wheel</defName>
    <label>Wheel</label>
    <description>A town on wheels and runners that circles the region once every few years, buying what others throw away and selling it back better. Wherever the Wheel stops there is welding by night and haggling by day, and by the time anyone gets used to it, it has moved on. They pay for scrap, mend what can be mended and rebuild what cannot.\n\nTheir ways began the night their valley burned. A wheelwright called Mab Wainwright put her house on her cart, her neighbours' children in the house and her tools on top, and drove out ahead of the fire; the others followed with whatever they could lift. Nobody has ever voted to stop. A Wheel hand still stitches a brass cog to the shoulder of the coat, and every coat is patched a dozen ways, because nothing on the Wheel is thrown away.\n\nThey talk fast, haggle hard and laugh about everything but fire. They will sell anything but the Wheel. Each yard is run by its yard boss, and the Wheel by its wheelwright, who alone says when it turns.</description>
    <pawnSingular>wheel hand</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>wheel hands</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>wheelwright</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Wheel_Hand</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Wheel</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_WheelTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/Wheel</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/WheelTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.52, 0.44, 0.18)</li>
      <li>(0.72, 0.62, 0.30)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
